
# ^ <type>[(<scope>)][!]: <subject>   imperative, max 72 chars, no full stop
#   e.g. fix(scan-list): correct pagination offset   or   fix: correct pagination offset
#   (scope) optional; ! = breaking change
#
# Body: what changed and why (not how). Wrap at 72.
#
# Trailers, last paragraph, one per line:
#   Refs: #123               optional here; the PR body carries it to main
#   Requirement: PRS-DP-1 SEC-001  regulated repos; qualify bare IDs with their document
#   Risk-Control: RC-TD-005        regulated repos, when applicable
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <what breaks>  optional, explains a ! in the subject
#
# Types: feat fix test refactor perf style docs build ci chore revert
#   feat           new or changed requirement
#   fix            defect (Refs the bug issue)
#   chore(deps)    dependency change (tick SOUP in the PR)
#   chore(release) version bump, release prep
#   type!: / type(scope)!:  breaking change, e.g. feat(api)!: drop v1 routes
#                  (release tooling bumps the version)
#
# Full rules: WI-19 Git & GitHub Conventions (QMS)
